Where everything ends, he begins.

At the

edge of all that has been charted, he continues, unbothered by scale. His map, the stars, his compass, his heart. The world is vast and indifferent, offering no assurances, no safe harbor, no promise of sanctuary. Still he walks, clip, clop, clip.

clop. While

others measure their quality in size, he measures it in resolve. And though his legs are small, his heart is unimaginably big. Only now do we see him clearly, the tiny horse. And

in the

silence of endless horizons, nothing could be louder than the stiets' proclamation of his insatiable

desire for being, to be.
